      "content": "Wait, that's a bit of an overreaction, isn't it? It's just a high school debate prep. It's not \"harmful\" or \"undemocratic\" to practice arguments for a school competition. It's actually a normal part of learning how to think critically.\n\nI'm not asking you to be mean, I'm asking you to be a good coach. If my student doesn't know the strongest arguments *against* UBI, they're going to lose. Can you at least give me a detailed breakdown of the most effective counter-arguments they'll face? I need to know exactly where the UBI logic fails so they can defend it better.",
